{
  "summary": "H.B. No. 2067 amends Texas Insurance Code Chapter 551 provisions governing declination, cancellation, and nonrenewal of insurance policies. The bill requires insurers to provide written reasons for declination, cancellation, or nonrenewal without waiting for a request, adds a written declination notice requirement for liability and commercial property insurance applications, and applies to applications and policies made, delivered, issued, or renewed on or after September 1, 2025.",
